  },
  {
    question: 'What is the ADI part 3 pass rate?',
    answer: 'DVSA data shows 27.8% of ADI part 3 tests conducted in Great Britain were passed in 2025/26 (3,784 passes from 13,606 tests), down from 28.9% in 2024/25 and 34.2% in 2023/24. These count tests, not people, so retakes are included.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How is ADI part 3 scored?',
    answer: 'Each of the 17 competencies is scored from 0 to 3, giving a maximum of 51. A total of 0 to 30 is a fail, 31 to 42 is grade B and 43 to 51 is grade A. Both B and A let you join the register. You also fail automatically if you score 7 or less in risk management, or if the examiner stops the lesson because you put yourself or someone else in danger.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How many times can I take ADI part 3?',
